Admit a subloop child and its parent link in one transaction; record the child finish once (#320) (#375)
Closes #320 and #321.

A subloop child, its initial thread and run.queued commit together with the parent's child_run.started, so a crash leaves both or neither and recovery reuses the same child; a child's completion is written in the same append as the parent's outcome, and a wake bound to the child's terminal sequence decides when an outcome is consumed. An interrupted script dispatch fails as resumable SCRIPT_OUTCOME_UNCERTAIN with its visit and dispatch provenance and runs again only on an explicit Resume or Replay; a forced stop keeps its non-resumable cause. The script-recovery browser check runs in the required Browser job. ADR-0046, ADR-0059.

Merged on the capped review path (D-035, D-042): three adversarial scans (the last returned delivery-hygiene blockers only, now fixed), independent behaviour QA passed, CI green at this head.

